    "created_at": "2026-01-08T16:09:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-08T16:09:54Z",
    "body": "The CSS Working Group just discussed `Revert \"Switch dialog/popover to using place-self:dialog\"`, and agreed to the following:\n\n* `SUMMARY: popover alignment tests are still valid because CSS added a rule to zero out auto margins`\n\n<details><summary>The full IRC log of that discussion</summary>\n&lt;dbaron> ScribeNick: domfarolino<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: based on Joey's analysis, we can revert the change to the HTML spec. someone plz review.<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: I still think some tests were added and some were kept and others were reverted. For the kept text, is there any spec text backing them up? were they based on prior specified things? Nobody has answered that question.<br>\n&lt;jarhar> https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/55116/changes#diff-ea4bb6fddd224701e36bddc57b641f805d930406d3356fae8f54278551fd96fb<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: Checking understanding. Asking about the html popover tests that are checking whether alignment responds correctly, right? Checking it as layout thing, rather than dialog?<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: I think those were the only tests that were not reverted, yeah<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: valid beause we're using a differentt mechanism: position-area property, auto margins are set to 0<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: Jake Archibald posted a rant about how confusing prior behavior is. Have to do something. Auto margins are set to 0 when using position-area. That enabled us to turn off the centering behavior in HTML. Not ideal, but it's what we've got since we can't change how popover has been implemented in UA stylesheet, due to compat<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: Test behavior is still correct, it's just based on the anchor positioning spec<br>\n&lt;fantasai> https://www.w3.org/TR/css-anchor-position-1/#position-area<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: OK. There was no change needed to HTML, even though these are popvoer tests?<br>\n&lt;fantasai> \"The used value of any auto inset properties and auto margin properties resolves to 0.\"<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: Correct. No changes needed besides reverting<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: CSS also doesn't define default style sheet for this thing; it's just based on position-area right?<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> fantasai: Yes. People tried to use position-area to align something to an anchor, but it would break because auto margins. So we forcibly shut that off.<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> annevk: next time, hopefully people leave a clearer paper trail and revert their own changes in the future<br>\n&lt;domfarolino> ScribeNick: jarhar<br>\n&lt;fantasai> SUMMARY: popover alignment tests are still valid because CSS added a rule to zero out auto margins<br>\n</details>\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
